a  lot of frustrating things so let's talk  about politics for a second there's a  bit of a Democratic surge it would seem  in Arizona you're trailing your opponent  in in your Senate race Joe Biden seems  to be doing well against President Trump  there according to polls is there a  democratic surge in Arizona and if so  what's behind it well I look  like this could be the last year of my  life I learned that when I lost my dad  at the age of 12 I talked about that in  there to fly and so I'm doing everything  I can in this unprecedented time to help  Arizonans in order to get the relief  that they need to get through this  there's a big fight ahead and there's  gonna be an important choice I would say  in my race the question of who is going  to take on China is going to be very  significant I have never trusted a  communist in my life my opponent  actually has been invested by the  Chinese Communist Party and and  companies and he's invested in them I'm  gonna take them on and confront them and  I think going forward the voters will  hear more about their choice in front of  them all right well as you say it could  be the last year of your life is the way  you live it and politically speaking  that may be true let's get into the book  a little bit you you've you've made it  through so much in your life that you  say you have something called a misery  database that you draw on to get through  adversity what is a misery database  well I shared this story in dare to fly  when I was climbing Mount Kilimanjaro  with some friends and one of her brought  his son and he was an elite athlete he  was really struggling and I just shared  that the rest of us we've been through a  lot of difficult times and to put one  foot in front of the other we were  tapping into that misery database to  give us strength to get through this  challenge and his database was empty but  he was building it at that moment and if  he could just get to the top of the  mountain it could propel him to do  amazing things in his life and he made  it and he's moved on to do incredible  things and I think for all of us we can  either reach back to our tough times and  we can have it pull us down and hold us  back or we can tap in and it can give us  resolve and strength and I talked about  that in my book all right senator  mcsalley  thank you very much I do want to  underscore one other point you make in  the book and that you attach to the  corona virus and this national response  we're all going through right now and  that is the lesson that you've learned  to do things afraid don't wait for  perfect conditions don't wait for the  perfect answer don't wait for the  perfect moment that moment is now good  words to live by and Senator Max I'll be  in here today  exactly of the a time  dare to fly us and share their stories  with me - no it really is a wonderful  book people who are interested in  politics people who are interested in  aviation the military there's something  for everyone dare to fly is available in  bookstores today
 

